    "created_at": "2023-06-14T08:26:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-14T08:26:23Z",
    "body": "All browsers prevent `line-height` from applying to `optgroup` and `option` within `select`.\r\n\r\nChromium sets `line-height: inital !important` for `option` and `optgroup` in `select multiple` [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css;l=955?q=html.css&ss=chromium).\r\n\r\nGecko sets `line-height: normal !important` for `option` and `optgroup` [here](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/2d678a843ceab81e43f7ffb83212197dc10e944a/layout/style/res/forms.css#319,346), though is discussing to also limit this rule to `select multiple`.\r\n\r\nFor select dropdown and in WebKit, `line-height` has no apparent effect.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
